/// A camera move as an output option — the turntable of controller 0.2.0 generalised in 0.4.0 (docs 06, part B): the controller renders Frames outputs with the state's camera moved about the focal point — revolved by Degrees in total about the orbit axis, raised by ElevationDegrees in total about the camera's right axis, and moved toward or away from the focal point until its distance is DollyFactor times the start — at a fixed or an advancing data time (TimeMode). Every move is an output-side transform of the captured camera: no animation track in the state, one timestep in gives a showcase sequence out. The azimuth of output i of N is Degrees * i / N (the last output stops short of the first, so a 360° orbit loops); elevation and dolly progress as i / (N - 1) so the last output reaches the full move. With Oscillate every component sways instead: sin(2πi/N) / 2 of its total, back and forth around the captured framing, a seamless loop. The presets of a client (orbit, rise, spiral, approach, rock) are combinations of these members.
